# The images built from this repository take only a few files from the build
# context: scripts/carla/g0-probe.sh (installed as the carla-g0-probe health
# check in the CARLA toolchain image) and scripts/dataset-converter/convert.py
# (the entrypoint of the dataset converter). Everything else in those images
# comes from apt, the LLVM apt repository, an upstream release tarball, a pip
# install, a base image stage or the dotnet SDK stage.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole working tree. On the DGX that tree
# is about 966 GB (artifacts, data/models and engines, third_party engine
# checkouts), so `docker build` cannot even start and the image silently goes
# stale: the toolchain image in use was built 2026-09-14 while the Dockerfile had
# already moved on by 2026-09-25. Denying everything and re-allowing only what a
# Dockerfile reads keeps the context at a few megabytes and makes a clean rebuild
# possible again. tests/test_carla_image_context.py enforces the invariant that
# every context input of every Dockerfile stays included.
# See docs/carla-dgx-audit.md 9.88.
*
!scripts
!scripts/carla
!scripts/carla/g0-probe.sh
!scripts/dataset-converter
!scripts/dataset-converter/convert.py
!images
!images/carla-arm64
!images/carla-arm64/Dockerfile
!images/dataset-converter
!images/dataset-converter/Dockerfile
!images/navsim
!images/navsim/Dockerfile
!images/ros-tools
!images/ros-tools/Dockerfile
